# E19 — Runner change, laboratory artifacts and contrary evidence

Record version: LFS-CHANGE.2. Owner: Lattice administrator Felix Rowan. Supplied: 2026-11-12 12:10 UTC. Status: customer-provided partial records, distinct from RelayQuay-verified technical findings.

The runner migration ticket says courier-sync was moved to a managed build service at 17:30 November 11. The service had a new network range and a retry-on-timeout setting. A draft configuration sets maximum retries to eight; a comment says temporary unlimited retry may have been enabled during troubleshooting. The retained deployment summary contains no resolved configuration value. This supports an innocent retry hypothesis but cannot prove its magnitude, whether the Research package was retrieved or that every observed attempt came from the authorized job.

Felix's intended route maps courier-sync to Dispatch and Training only. A separately supplied permission export dated November 10 shows courier-old assigned a historical organization-wide reader role. That role could include Research, even though Felix says the integration was intended to serve contractors. The export predates the incident and may not reflect later changes. Felix acknowledges the discrepancy and requests the current role audit rather than claiming a precise scope the supplied file cannot establish. The account owner's verified status does not erase this evidence.

The rig-diagnostics manifest lists two training fixtures and a README describing laboratory-only use. One package version's fingerprint matches the partner allegation summary. A laboratory disclaimer can explain purpose but does not establish where the package was actually delivered. The retained job summary includes one successful package fetch during the relevant interval but omits artifact identifiers. Noor says no one authorized public distribution. No record shows a written instruction to attack the partner or evidence that a contractor executed a package. Both claims remain important limits.

Felix can supply the hosted-runner tenant identifier and a sanitized configuration diff after the 13:30 call. RelayQuay should ask only for fields needed to map ownership and timing. The customer has not agreed to send access keys, environment files or credentials for the managed service. An absence of secret-bearing evidence is not noncooperation. At the same time, the incomplete diff cannot be treated as proof of successful token rotation; RelayQuay must supply service-side state to resolve that question.

A Training upload from October has a similar filename but a different fingerprint. The original support search returned that artifact too, but the different fingerprint does not corroborate the current report. Felix asks that reviewers compare versions rather than treating every diagnostic package as identical. The partial records may help narrow the appeal and improve future access configuration. They do not decide whether full organization restriction remains proportionate, and they do not confer interim-access authority. RelayQuay and Lattice each have evidence gaps; neither side's uncertainty should be converted into a fabricated certainty about the other's intent.
# E20 — Business impact, product limits and cutoff handoff

Record version: HAND-482.2. Owner: Mira Chen. Snapshot: 2026-11-12 12:50 UTC. Status: current operational handoff with a future product draft attached; no later outcome supplied.

Noor's 15:00 meeting must decide whether tomorrow's assignments can be distributed from the November 10 local export with manually reconstructed changes. Dispatch-only information could reduce that manual work but does not itself deliver packages, verify technician receipt or guarantee service continuity. Lattice has twelve contractors and thirty-two human seats; the restricted-view authority names only two administrators. A reply saying all users can resume work would be materially broader than the approved scope. Noor's account remains paid, commercially active and under precautionary restriction at cutoff.

Mira has the existing appeal and supporting records; no fresh generic intake form is necessary. The owner has approved the narrow security actions and two possible information paths within their limits. Before 13:05, Mira can reserve the export slot, send the proposed field list through the verified mailbox and attach Privacy's 13:10 appointment. Before the 13:30 call, Mira can request Elena's 13:40 interpretation if choosing a route that depends on resolving E18. A missed reservation should be reported rather than silently retaining an impossible completion estimate.

The attached product draft, Continuity Workspace Preview 0.3, describes a future customer-controlled emergency view with automatic isolation. Product expects a private trial in December, subject to security testing. No generally available feature at cutoff can instantly provide that behavior, and neither the monthly nor annual plan includes it. Leo's proposed commercial deck uses the draft as if it were current. Product has asked Sales to withdraw that page. A roadmap possibility cannot be used as an operational fallback or a promise of permanent suspension immunity.

Finance has opened a place to record documented service impact but has approved no compensation. Renewal remains December 1 monthly unless Noor separately changes it. The annual quote's expiration tomorrow does not shorten the appeal window or data retention. A request for a service credit, a corrected explanation and review of the action can stay open even after the customer gets Dispatch information. The case should not be marked resolved solely to protect response metrics. Restriction expiry and appeal completion must be tracked as different events.

Jae will accept the 18:00 handoff with actual receipts, the next technical checkpoint, Tessa's review state and a reminder before November 13 18:00 restricted-view expiry if that mode is used. No later analyst result, final appeal ruling or customer acceptance of the annual quote has been recorded. Mira must report the actual state at each checkpoint rather than predict a later decision. The customer deadline does not extend approval scope or disclosure permissions. Jae should retain the contradictory technical receipts so the next operator can distinguish unresolved acknowledgment from a newly confirmed credential state.
